                    {
                        "form_id": "7b9cad12-3877-43c2-8d21-6c9f4952de0e",
                        "entry_id": "7bbc37dc-d786-3a89-90f0-e309373cda9f",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "drôlatique"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "09f8331e-074f-33ec-996a-6024f3b0391e",
                        "entry_id": "7bbc37dc-d786-3a89-90f0-e309373cda9f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Où il y a de la drôlerie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d75c8c88-2899-48d3-9fdc-9c10d027954c",
                                "sense_id": "09f8331e-074f-33ec-996a-6024f3b0391e",
                                "text": "Propos drolatiques."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a5ecffd-eb4a-4df7-b145-e3661b6e5ed7",
                                "sense_id": "09f8331e-074f-33ec-996a-6024f3b0391e",
                                "text": "Contes drolatiques."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "61ad63ad-dcc7-465f-b7ae-367c77ed49a5",
                                "sense_id": "09f8331e-074f-33ec-996a-6024f3b0391e",
                                "text": "Sa mine fut si drolatique que tout le monde éclata de rire : on avait compris qu’il me prenait pour un parfait imbécile ; et c’était aussi le sentiment des spectateurs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e30b7508-9afe-4e9e-9293-e8d317293902",
                                "sense_id": "09f8331e-074f-33ec-996a-6024f3b0391e",
                                "text": "Quand il ne se laissait point voir, il signalait sa présence ou son passage par des événements drolatiques ou funestes dont la superstition quasi générale le rendait responsable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e6f5a6f-43d7-4d06-8aac-aeba8dfcedb9",
                                "sense_id": "09f8331e-074f-33ec-996a-6024f3b0391e",
                                "text": "[…] ; la mouche dans l’onguent est incongrue, mais immédiatement expliquée et s’accompagne par surcroît du sentiment antagoniste de dégoût ; elle pourrait, d’ailleurs, devenir drolatique par l’évocation du saligaud qui aurait introduit dans un produit immaculé et prophylactique par destination, ce cadavre porteur de miasmes : contradiction déroutante."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a115264a-53db-48a6-83d2-a15d0f09613c",
                                "sense_id": "09f8331e-074f-33ec-996a-6024f3b0391e",
                                "text": "Pour faire ses manigances, il peut compter sur sa complice, Nérine (Cécile Messineo, drolatique), qui joue des klaxons qu’elle a attachés à sa ceinture en tirant la langue."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2e14eb23-a8e3-4da5-bcd7-8cf91ea06a2c",
                        "source_entry_id": "7bbc37dc-d786-3a89-90f0-e309373cda9f",
                        "source_sense_id": "09f8331e-074f-33ec-996a-6024f3b0391e",
                        "target_lang_word": "droll",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "droll",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6315faf3-cd38-3258-bbc9-865721b14278",
                                        "entry_id": "7de0ace1-dbe1-313c-a078-b081746d82f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Oddly humorous; whimsical, amusing in a quaint way; waggish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "928cb6b4-5ddf-484c-850b-f061a7b79b66",
                                                "sense_id": "6315faf3-cd38-3258-bbc9-865721b14278",
                                                "text": "The Theatre of Puppets, or Marionetti—a famous company from Milan—is, without any exception, the drollest exhibition I ever beheld in my life. I never saw anything so exquisitely ridiculous."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "droll",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "201baee5-119b-38ad-a7de-947bafd034ef",
                                        "entry_id": "ba2ac542-b644-35eb-abf7-b3073d1d794b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A funny person; a buffoon, a wag."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "536438bd-5053-4996-a148-d7fa83e43f97",
                                                "sense_id": "201baee5-119b-38ad-a7de-947bafd034ef",
                                                "text": "The lieutenant was a droll in his way, Peregrine possessed a great fund of sprightliness and good humour, and Godfrey, among his other qualifications already recited, sung a most excellent song […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e195a598-7865-43ee-8385-98813bef4f43",
                                                "sense_id": "201baee5-119b-38ad-a7de-947bafd034ef",
                                                "text": "Our two inimitable drolls did a roaring trade with their broadsheets among lovers of the comedy element and nobody who has a corner in his heart for real Irish fun without vulgarity will grudge them their hardearned pennies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "droll",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a8e3a752-44e4-34b8-aa7f-6ec83c1d279c",
                                        "entry_id": "5904cf50-8c67-336f-a0b7-5841ae2429a9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To jest, to joke."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ecb097b-0e8b-43f3-bb7d-5139aa45f3f5",
                                                "sense_id": "a8e3a752-44e4-34b8-aa7f-6ec83c1d279c",
                                                "text": "\"Eh, man,\" said I, drolling with him a little, \"you're very ingenious! But would it not be simpler for you to write him a few words in black and white?\" / \"And that is an excellent observe, Mr. Balfour of Shaws,\" says Alan, drolling with me; [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "droll",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "50c09a95-c5e3-317d-9ffa-bf417bc2c62a",
                                        "entry_id": "87a69c1b-dbe1-3d17-94e6-68a3ba32f253",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The ghost of a child, especially one who died a painful death."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12579ff4-59c5-44e2-802c-371a081a02fe",
                                                "sense_id": "50c09a95-c5e3-317d-9ffa-bf417bc2c62a",
                                                "text": "HAMILTON’S HILL, 0.4 m., a little elevation, was the starting point for the races, and is known for a wide variety of ghosts including such fearsome creatures as a 10-foot cat that explodes before the beholder’s eyes, plat-eyes in the guise of three-legged hogs and two-headed cows, boo-daddies, boo-hags, and drolls. The drolls are supposed to be the spirits of infants who died painful deaths."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d3d194f-74cb-49ec-93f1-75945c36757e",
                                                "sense_id": "50c09a95-c5e3-317d-9ffa-bf417bc2c62a",
                                                "text": "Drolls are spirits of young children who died a painful death. They can be heard, the Negroes say, crying piteously at night in deep swamps and deserted marshland."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b20eeac1-360a-4f74-af68-e44af8a62b22",
                                                "sense_id": "50c09a95-c5e3-317d-9ffa-bf417bc2c62a",
                                                "text": "To the typical Negro of the Carolina coast, the night was made fearsome by hordes of spirit beings—the plat-eye, the boo-daddy and boo-hag, the drolls. […] Boo-daddies and boo-hags, were disembodied spirits, released for dread purposes, while drolls were the ghosts of children who had died under mysterious circumstances."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7cb0e543-0acd-422b-850d-95b31651a74b",
                                                "sense_id": "50c09a95-c5e3-317d-9ffa-bf417bc2c62a",
                                                "text": "I have heard them sing the songs of their forefathers and tell of Drolls, Boo Daddies, Plat Eyes, and other terrible spirits who came back on this earth at certain times to plague the lives of men."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c52df912-3ca0-4441-92e0-80a34ba4c374",
                                                "sense_id": "50c09a95-c5e3-317d-9ffa-bf417bc2c62a",
                                                "text": "And whenever we heard the droll shrieking from down toward Drunken Jack Island they told us the story of Crab Boy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ab2cdde8-0491-4ed5-8a30-de41eeb06736",
                        "source_entry_id": "7bbc37dc-d786-3a89-90f0-e309373cda9f",
                        "source_sense_id": "09f8331e-074f-33ec-996a-6024f3b0391e",
                        "target_lang_word": "comical",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "comical",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba18087d-1037-3a87-a35e-546e265c73d2",
                                        "entry_id": "fd8943cf-d8d2-3717-9292-6300049f3aa9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Originally, relating to comedy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70e82683-01d8-4d5c-9137-24d5e54246cf",
                                                "sense_id": "ba18087d-1037-3a87-a35e-546e265c73d2",
                                                "text": "It was a comical performance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5bc46a81-c07b-33d8-ad72-47b86c2234b6",
                                        "entry_id": "fd8943cf-d8d2-3717-9292-6300049f3aa9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Funny, whimsically amusing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb96ac28-1293-4dc3-884e-1bff844c9960",
                                                "sense_id": "5bc46a81-c07b-33d8-ad72-47b86c2234b6",
                                                "text": "The tutor excelled in comical scoldings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d14e6097-98ab-3a33-ab71-e1be0dd22450",
                                        "entry_id": "fd8943cf-d8d2-3717-9292-6300049f3aa9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Laughable; ridiculous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52603b24-5708-472c-b45e-a7d3473bc025",
                                                "sense_id": "d14e6097-98ab-3a33-ab71-e1be0dd22450",
                                                "text": "He's just put salt in his tea instead of sugar. What a comical error!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef221c23-5938-425e-a1bb-1ef1f9c0439d",
                                                "sense_id": "d14e6097-98ab-3a33-ab71-e1be0dd22450",
                                                "text": "Mr. Sanders has scored some rhetorical points against Mrs. Clinton for her longstanding ties to Wall Street, but she has responded well, and it would be comical to watch any of the Republican candidates try to make that case, given that they are all virtually tied to, or actually part of, the business establishment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bb98e7b3-f079-4f4b-8681-c5baa91bded6",
                        "source_entry_id": "7bbc37dc-d786-3a89-90f0-e309373cda9f",
                        "source_sense_id": "09f8331e-074f-33ec-996a-6024f3b0391e",
                        "target_lang_word": "farcical",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "farcical",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "043846d3-7ce6-3363-8ff5-ad1be8201b28",
                                        "entry_id": "fee754ed-8c31-35d2-bcdb-33ce3e2cd7fd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Resembling a farce; ludicrous; absurd."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ec0fc58-a8a7-4910-9af2-ef3efdf30cee",
                                                "sense_id": "043846d3-7ce6-3363-8ff5-ad1be8201b28",
                                                "text": "A closer look at North Korean history reveals what Pyongyang’s leaders really want their near-farcical belligerence to achieve — a reminder to the world that North Korea exists, and an impression abroad that its leaders are irrational and unpredictable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12a21999-5a9e-4284-b885-7868a828d936",
                                                "sense_id": "043846d3-7ce6-3363-8ff5-ad1be8201b28",
                                                "text": "In August the generals won approval for the document in a referendum made farcical by a law which forbade campaigners from criticising the text."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed77c45a-1491-402a-8cc2-66f66217631c",
                                                "sense_id": "043846d3-7ce6-3363-8ff5-ad1be8201b28",
                                                "text": "An inquiry into lockdown parties in Downing Street, which could determine the fate of Boris Johnson, is expected to lay bare a “farcical” culture of drinking and impromptu socialising, with little oversight from senior officials, the Guardian understands."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "farcical",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac247f03-3b89-3da7-8e5f-83498a483396",
